you've all heard the phrase before can't  be the boss and bloodborne get good not  fast enough to out tonight someone in  battlefield get good shoelace is untied  get good people have used it jokingly  and sometimes seriously for a while and  the latest game to embody its sentiment  is none other than the colorful 1930s  cartoon inspired  cuphead people are calling it the dark  souls of platformers which is actually  quite fitting not just because you're  literally collecting the souls of your  enemies but also because of the game's  boss rush design everyone the bosses  presents unique challenges that will  test your skills reactions and  multitasking abilities they're comprised  of several different phases with each  phase posing new and completely  different obstacles than the last some  people might not find any enjoyment out  of dying over and over but for cuphead  that's the exact way the game should be  played if each boss had mechanics simple  enough to beat a blind in one go the  challenge obviously wouldn't be there  but more importantly the game would lack  the very real sense of accomplishment  and satisfaction that defeating one of  its many bosses gives you  the way each battle is structured  encourages you to die learn from your  mistakes and come back swinging in the  next rematch the game teaches you each  section slowly and once you've figured  out how to navigate the bullet hell in  one phase and are able to get past it  you immediately get the sense of  fulfillment it's very much like a really  good sneeze a satisfying release but you  are also left with a mess immediately  afterwards since the boss will change  things up and you'll have to learn the  next part in the same manner you can  call it masochism or whatever you want  but in my opinion the game never really  becomes a vehicle for frustration every  death takes you immediately back to the  start no loading required and the  tantalizing thought of completing the  level is teased with the timeline  tracking your progress yes you may die  to a boss several dozen times over and  over retry after every stupid mistake as  you slowly lose track of time and  suddenly it's 4 a.m. and you should  definitely be sleeping but I mean in all  fairness time is just a human construct  put in place to keep people like us from  playing more Cup head  [Music]  maybe the best way to describe the game  would be difficult but fair as hazards  rarely if ever feel unavoidable there  can be a lot of moving parts within each  encounter and even if there are a bunch  of things going on at once they each  tend to be straightforward and  consistent for example this one blimp  will always spit out a single projectile  at you while this other blimp will  always spit out several in the same  pattern and the boss will always laugh  in the same direction so these things  alone are easily avoidable but when you  combine them all you have a recipe for  the scathing difficulty that becomes a  lifeblood of the entire game but unlike  some other games that are difficult just  for difficulties sake couple approaches  the dreaded trial and error concept with  Grace and finesse and never once  punishes you for doing the right thing  you may die to a stray ghosts eyeball or  a razor-sharp feather but unlike you and  your skill those things never change  between fights figuring out the bosses  mechanics on your own applying them and  taking them down because you had the  spatial awareness to avoid all the crap  thrown at you is what the game is all  about the learning process may be  daunting for some but when you succeed  it's a supremely gratifying and  immensely rewarding experience that  makes all the deaths that came before it  or at the time  [Music]  hey guys I hope you liked this short  take on Cup heads difficulty it's one of  my personal favorites of the entire year  and I hope that you find some time to at  least give it a shot even if it's not  your bag if you have played it I want to  hear about it in the comments below I  want to hear favorite bosses least  favorite bosses the most vs thing in the  game let me know what you think and  don't forget to check out the review of  the game over on GameSpot calm and I'll  see you guys next time  [Music]
 

